## Claim
Text: "Right after a time where we're going through a pandemic that lost 22 million jobs at the height, we've already added back 11.6 million jobs."
Claim author: Mike Pence 
Claim date: October 07, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### According to the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, what was the peak number of jobs lost in the United States during the COVID-19 pandemic recession in 2020?
Answer: According to the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics data cited in the search result, the peak number of jobs lost from mid-February to mid-April 2020 was 19.8 million private nonfarm jobs, representing a 15.4% decline from pre-pandemic employment levels.

Source URL: https://www.ncci.com/SecureDocuments/QEB/Insights_QEB_2020_Q2-COVIDEmployment.html

### In which specific month of 2020 did the U.S. economy reach the trough of job losses, representing the peak of pandemic-related unemployment?
Answer: April 2020, when the U.S. economy lost a record 20.5 million jobs, marking the trough of pandemic-related unemployment.

Source URL: https://blog.nic.org/record-decline-of-20.5-million-jobs-in-april

